  "question": {
    "text": "<p>If <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn></math> moles of an ideal gas expands from <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>10</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">L</mi></math> to a volume of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>100</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">L</mi></math> at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>300</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></math> under isothermal and reversible condition then work, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">w</mi></math>, is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi></math>. The value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>-</mo></math>_______.</p><p>(Given <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>.314</mo><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi><mo> </mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo> </mo><msup><mi>mol</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>)</p>"
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "-28721",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Given,</p><p> <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>300</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi><mo>,</mo><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"></mspace><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">L</mi><mo>,</mo><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"></mspace><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>100</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">L</mi><mo>,</mo><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"></mspace><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn></math></p><p>It is isothermal reversible expansion, so work done negative</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">W</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>.303</mo><mi>nRT</mi><mo> </mo><mi>log</mi><mfenced><mfrac><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mfrac></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>.303</mo><mo>×</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>×</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>.314</mo><mo>×</mo><mn>300</mn><mo> </mo><mi>log</mi><mfenced><mfrac><mn>100</mn><mn>10</mn></mfrac></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mo>−</mo><mn>28720</mn><mo>.713</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>≡</mo><mo>−</mo><mn>28721</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi></math></p>"
